WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:06.080
To Brazil, where more than 600,000&nbsp;
people have now died from COVID-19.&nbsp;

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:12.240
Activists in Rio de Janeiro displayed 600&nbsp;
white handkerchiefs in tribute to the victims.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:17.440
The memorial ceremony on Copacabana beach&nbsp;
was organized by the NGO Rio de Paz.&nbsp;

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:22.960
Many in Brazil blame President Jair Bolsonaro&nbsp;
for the deaths. Bolsonaro has consistently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:26.560
downplayed the danger caused&nbsp;
by the virus and anger at his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.675
handling of the pandemic is growing.
In Brazil, 600,000 people have now died&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.675 --> 00:00:29.767
from COVID-19 infections, the second highest&nbsp;
death rate in the world after the US. Brazil's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:29.849
President Jair Bolsonaro has repeatedly&nbsp;
downplayed the threat posed by the virus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.849 --> 00:00:29.944
and opposed measures like mask wearing, limiting&nbsp;
activity or encouraging vaccination. Brazil's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.944 --> 00:00:30.038
senate is investigating Bolsonaro for politicizing&nbsp;
the pandemic and failing to secure oxygen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.038 --> 00:00:30.115
and vaccines for the country. People&nbsp;
angry with the government's management,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.115 --> 00:00:32.640
have taken to the streets to call for change.
Frustration – taken to the streets of Brazilian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:38.240
cities. Directed mainly at the country's&nbsp;
corona-skeptic president, Jair Bolsonaro.&nbsp;

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:44.640
No country has been able to escape COVID&nbsp;
-19, but many here are angry that Brazil has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:51.440
lost so many lives. With 600,000, it's&nbsp;
the 2nd highest death rate worldwide.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:57.902
Per capital Brazil is among the top ten countries&nbsp;
suffering the greatest losses, leading the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.902 --> 00:01:00.320
demonstrators here to call for impeachment.
"This is a pandemic-denialist government,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:05.120
spreading a policy of death, whose economic&nbsp;
agenda has driven people to starvation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:11.840
We are in a desperate situation here,&nbsp;
and the President doesn't seem to care."&nbsp;

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:18.720
Even as Brazil dominated global headlines with&nbsp;
spikes in infections and images of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.120
mass graves shared around the world, Bolsonaro&nbsp;
didn't change his tune, calling the deadly virus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:30.880
"just a little flu" and minimizing the&nbsp;
strain and losses people were suffering from.&nbsp;

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:37.200
He has also repeatedly spoken out against mask&nbsp;
wearing and vaccines, while promoting unproven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:42.080
medicines for use by doctors -- including&nbsp;
recently in a speech at the United Nations.&nbsp;

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.880
"We respect the patient and doctor relationship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:50.640
with the decision on the medication to be&nbsp;
used and the potential for off-label use."&nbsp;

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:59.600
Within the government, there are also concerns.&nbsp;
For months, Brazil's senate has been investigating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:04.880
Bolsonaro's pandemic management, including the&nbsp;
use of taxpayer money to purchase experimental&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:10.240
medicines. Just last week, whistleblowers&nbsp;
detailed information about a hospital chain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:16.400
pushing the use of such off-label meds&nbsp;
on the elderly -- without their consent.&nbsp;

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:20.880
"So the doctors explained to me they gave the&nbsp;
COVID kit of meds to the patients and told them:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:26.960
'I have to give this to you, because if I don't,&nbsp;
they can fire me. But I can tell you that if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:32.160
take anything from here, take only the proteins&nbsp;
and the vitamins, because the other medicines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:37.680
besides having no efficacy, can be very&nbsp;
dangerous, specifically for the elderly.'"&nbsp;

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:47.840
Bolsonaro's approval rating has slipped to just&nbsp;
22-percent. But not everyone has criticism for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:53.920
the president. On September 7, large crowds came&nbsp;
out to show support for Bolsonaro on National Day.&nbsp;

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:00.240
But as the pandemic continues to take lives,&nbsp;
several local governments are moving forward&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:07.360
with their push to vaccinate, even extending&nbsp;
shots now to young people. More than 200&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:17.840
municipalities are also introducing a vaccine&nbsp;
passport - which Bolsonaro strongly opposes.

